{"book": "gate-da", "num": 10, "label": "10", "slug": "10-matrices-rank-and-nullity", "title": "Rank and Nullity", "tag": "Matrices & Linear Algebra", "summary": "A vector can be seen as a matrix with either a single row or a single column:", "wordCount": 822, "readingTimeMin": 4, "intro": [], "sections": [{"id": "10.1", "title": "Vectors from Matrices", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "A <b>vector</b> can be seen as a matrix with either a single row or a single column:"}, {"t": "p", "x": "1. A <b>column vector</b> is an $n \\times 1$ matrix:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{bmatrix}v_1 \\\\ v_2 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ v_n\\end{bmatrix}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "2. A <b>row vector</b> is a $1 \\times n$ matrix:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{bmatrix}u_1 & u_2 & \\dots & u_n\\end{bmatrix}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Thus, vectors can be viewed as special cases of matrices with either one column or one row."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "34", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Column vector from matrix:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\in \\mathbb{R}^3"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "35", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Row vector from matrix:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\in \\mathbb{R}^4"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "36", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "A $2 \\times 1$ matrix can be treated as a vector in $\\mathbb{R}^2$:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mathbf{w} = \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "37", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "A $1 \\times 5$ matrix as a row vector:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mathbf{x} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}"}]}]}, {"id": "10.2", "title": "Row Space, Column Space, and Null Space", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "For a matrix $A \\in \\mathbb{R}^{m \\times n}$:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The <b>row space</b> of $A$, denoted $\\text{Row}(A)$, is the subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^n$ spanned by the row vectors of $A$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The <b>column space</b> of $A$, denoted $\\text{Col}(A)$, is the subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^m$ spanned by the column vectors of $A$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The <b>null space</b> (or kernel) of $A$, denoted $\\text{Null}(A)$, is the set of all $x \\in \\mathbb{R}^n$ such that $Ax = 0$."}]}]}, {"t": "p", "x": "These spaces are fundamental because they reveal the structure of the solutions of linear systems."}]}, {"t": "h", "level": 3, "x": "Prerequisites: Echelon Forms", "id": "prerequisites-echelon-forms"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Before finding these subspaces, we need to understand the concept of <b>echelon forms</b>."}, {"t": "box", "kind": "definition", "name": "Definition", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Row Echelon Form (REF)</b> of a matrix $A$ is a form that satisfies:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": true, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "All non-zero rows are above rows of all zeros."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The leading (first non-zero) entry of each row, called a <b>pivot</b>, is to the right of the pivot in the row above it."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "All entries below a pivot are zeros."}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "definition", "name": "Definition", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Column Echelon Form (CEF)</b> is similar to REF but applied to columns:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": true, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "All non-zero columns are to the left of all-zero columns."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The topmost non-zero entry in each pivot column is above the pivot entry in the column to its right."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "All entries to the right of a pivot in its row are zeros."}]}]}]}, {"t": "h", "level": 3, "x": "Finding the Spaces", "id": "finding-the-spaces"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Row Space:</b> Reduce $A$ to REF using row operations. The non-zero rows of the REF form a basis for $\\text{Row}(A)$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Column Space:</b> The pivot columns of the <i>original matrix</i> $A$ form a basis for $\\text{Col}(A)$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Null Space:</b> Solve the homogeneous system $Ax=0$ using the REF to find free variables. The solution vectors form a basis for $\\text{Null}(A)$."}]}]}, {"t": "h", "level": 3, "x": "Example 1: Row, Column, and Null Spaces", "id": "example-1-row-column-and-null-spaces"}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "38", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Find the row space, column space, and null space."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\nPerform row reduction step-by-step:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\end{bmatrix} \n\\overset{R_2-2R_1,\\ R_3-R_1}{\\longrightarrow}\n\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 \\end{bmatrix}\n\\overset{-R_3}{\\longrightarrow}\n\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\end{bmatrix}\n\\overset{\\text{swap } R_2 \\leftrightarrow R_3}{\\longrightarrow}\n\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Row Space:</b>\nNon-zero rows form a basis:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\text{Row}(A) = \\text{span}\\{ [1,2,3], [0,1,2] \\}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Column Space:</b>\nThe pivot columns (1st and 2nd) of the <i>original</i> matrix form a basis:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\text{Col}(A) = \\text{span}\\left\\{ \n\\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix}, \n\\begin{bmatrix} 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix} \n\\right\\}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Null Space:</b>\nFrom REF, equations are:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "x_1 + 2x_2 + 3x_3 = 0, \\quad x_2 + 2x_3 = 0."}, {"t": "p", "x": "From the second equation, $x_2 = -2x_3$. Substituting into the first:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "x_1 + 2(-2x_3) + 3x_3 = 0 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad x_1 = x_3."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Let $x_3 = t$, then the solution vector is:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "x = t \\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Thus,"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\text{Null}(A) = \\text{span}\\left\\{ \\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix} \\right\\}."}]}, {"t": "h", "level": 3, "x": "Example 2: Already in Row Echelon Form", "id": "example-2-already-in-row-echelon-form"}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "39", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\nSince $A$ is already in REF, we directly identify:"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Row Space:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\text{Row}(A) = \\text{span}\\{[1,0,2],[0,1,3]\\}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Column Space:</b>\nPivot columns are the first and second columns:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\text{Col}(A) = \\text{span}\\left\\{ \n\\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix},\n\\begin{bmatrix} 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix} \n\\right\\}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Null Space:</b>\nFrom equations:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "x_1 + 2x_3 = 0, \\quad x_2 + 3x_3 = 0."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Let $x_3 = t$. Then $x_1 = -2t$, $x_2 = -3t$, so"}, {"t": "math", "x": "x = t \\begin{bmatrix} -2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Thus,"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\text{Null}(A) = \\text{span}\\left\\{ \\begin{bmatrix} -2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix} \\right\\}."}]}]}, {"id": "10.3", "title": "Rank of a Matrix", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The <b>rank</b> of a matrix $A$ is the dimension of its row space (or equivalently its column space).\nIt equals the number of leading $1$s (pivots) in the row echelon form of $A$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "40", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Find the rank of"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9 \\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Reduce:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9 \\end{bmatrix} \n\\sim \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -12 \\end{bmatrix}\n\\sim \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Two pivots $\\implies \\text{rank}(A)=2$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "41", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Find the rank of"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 6 \\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Second row = $2 \\times$ first row. Only one independent row."}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\text{rank}(A)=1."}]}]}, {"id": "10.4", "title": "Properties of Rank", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "list", "ordered": true, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\text{rank}(A) \\leq \\min(m,n)$ for an $m \\times n$ matrix $A$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\text{rank}(A) = \\text{rank}(A^T)$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\text{rank}(AB) \\leq \\min(\\text{rank}(A), \\text{rank}(B))$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If $A$ is invertible ($n \\times n$), then $\\text{rank}(A)=n$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If $A$ has a zero row (or column), removing it does not change rank."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$\\text{rank}(A+B) \\leq \\text{rank}(A) + \\text{rank}(B)$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If $A$ is diagonal/triangular, then $\\text{rank}(A)$ is the number of nonzero diagonal entries."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Elementary row/column operations do not change the rank of a matrix."}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "42", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Property 1:</b> For $A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$,\n$\\min(m,n) = \\min(2,3)=2$. Reducing,"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\begin{bmatrix}1&2&3\\\\4&5&6\\end{bmatrix} \\sim \n\\begin{bmatrix}1&2&3\\\\0&-3&-6\\end{bmatrix}\n\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}1&2&3\\\\0&1&2\\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Two pivots $\\implies \\text{rank}(A)=2 \\leq 2$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "43", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Property 2:</b> For $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1&2\\\\3&6\\\\4&8\\end{bmatrix}$,\nrow 2 = $3\\times$row 1, row 3 = $4\\times$row 1, so $\\text{rank}(A)=1$.\nNow $A^T=\\begin{bmatrix}1&3&4\\\\2&6&8\\end{bmatrix}$, col 2 = $3\\times$col 1, col 3 = $4\\times$col 1, so $\\text{rank}(A^T)=1$.\nThus, $\\text{rank}(A)=\\text{rank}(A^T)=1$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "44", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Property 3:</b> Let"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A=\\begin{bmatrix}1&0\\\\0&0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0&0\\\\0&1\\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Here, $\\text{rank}(A)=1$, $\\text{rank}(B)=1$. But"}, {"t": "math", "x": "AB=\\begin{bmatrix}1&0\\\\0&0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0&0\\\\0&1\\end{bmatrix}\n= \\begin{bmatrix}0&0\\\\0&0\\end{bmatrix},"}, {"t": "p", "x": "so $\\text{rank}(AB)=0 \\leq \\min(1,1)$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "45", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Property 4:</b> If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2&1\\\\5&3\\end{bmatrix}$,"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\det(A)=2\\cdot3 - 5\\cdot1 = 1 \\neq 0."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Hence $A$ invertible, $\\text{rank}(A)=2$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "46", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Property 5:</b> $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1&2&3\\\\4&5&6\\\\0&0&0\\end{bmatrix}$.\nRemoving the zero row gives $\\begin{bmatrix}1&2&3\\\\4&5&6\\end{bmatrix}$, which has the same rank ($=2$)."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "47", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Property 6:</b> Let"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A=\\begin{bmatrix}1&0\\\\0&0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0&0\\\\0&1\\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "$\\text{rank}(A)=1$, $\\text{rank}(B)=1$. Then"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A+B=\\begin{bmatrix}1&0\\\\0&1\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad \\text{rank}(A+B)=2."}, {"t": "p", "x": "So $\\text{rank}(A+B)=2 \\leq 1+1=2$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "48", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Property 7:</b> For triangular $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2&5&1\\\\0&3&7\\\\0&0&0\\end{bmatrix}$,\nthe nonzero diagonal entries are $2,3$. So $\\text{rank}(A)=2$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "49", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Property 8:</b> $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1&2\\\\3&6\\end{bmatrix}$.\nRow 2 = $3\\times$ row 1, so $\\text{rank}(A)=1$.\nApply row operation $R_2 \\to R_2 - 3R_1$:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\begin{bmatrix}1&2\\\\0&0\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad \\text{rank}=1."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Rank is unchanged."}]}]}, {"id": "10.5", "title": "Nullity of a Matrix", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The <b>nullity</b> of $A \\in \\mathbb{R}^{m \\times n}$ is the dimension of its null space.\nIt measures how many free variables there are in the system $Ax=0$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "50", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Find nullity of"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 6 \\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Row rank = 1, matrix has $n=3$ columns.\nBy rank-nullity: $\\text{nullity}(A) = 3-1=2$.\nIndeed, $x_1 + 2x_2 + 3x_3=0$ gives two free variables, basis:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\text{Null}(A) = \\text{span}\\left\\{ \\begin{bmatrix}-2\\\\1\\\\0\\end{bmatrix}, \\begin{bmatrix}-3\\\\0\\\\1\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "51", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Find nullity of"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Rank=2, $n=3$.\nNullity = $3-2=1$. Null space = span$\\{[-2,-3,1]\\}$."}]}]}, {"id": "10.6", "title": "Rank-Nullity Theorem", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Rank-Nullity Theorem:</b> For any $A \\in \\mathbb{R}^{m \\times n}$,"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\text{rank}(A) + \\text{nullity}(A) = n."}, {"t": "p", "x": "This balances the number of pivot variables (rank) and free variables (nullity)."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "52", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Verify rank-nullity for"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Rank = 2 (row-reduced form has 2 pivots).\nNullity = $3-2=1$.\nCheck: $2+1=3=n$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "53", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Verify rank-nullity for"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 \\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Second row = 2×first row $=>$rank=1.\n$n=3$ $=>$nullity=$3-1=2$.\nCheck: $1+2=3=n$."}]}]}, {"id": "10.7", "title": "Applications of Rank and Nullity", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Applications:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": true, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Consistency of systems:</b> $Ax=b$ is consistent iff $\\text{rank}(A)=\\text{rank}([A|b])$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Invertibility:</b> $A$ is invertible iff $\\text{rank}(A)=n$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Linear dependence:</b> Rank tells maximum independent rows/columns."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Geometry:</b> Null space gives directions squashed to zero; column space gives range of transformation."}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "54", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Solve"}, {"t": "math", "x": "x+y+z=6,\\quad 2x+2y+2z=12,\\quad x+y+2z=7."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>\nCoefficient matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1&1&1\\\\2&2&2\\\\1&1&2\\end{bmatrix}$.\nRow reduce $=>$rank$(A)=2$, rank$([A|b])=2$ $=>$system consistent.\n$n=3$, nullity=$1$ $=>$infinitely many solutions, parameterized by one free variable."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "55", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Check if $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$ is invertible.\n<b>Solution:</b> Rank$(A)=2$, $n=2$. Rank = number of columns $=>$invertible.\nIndeed, $\\det(A)=-2\\neq 0$."}]}]}], "sectionCount": 7}